.policy "ruff-d102-undocumented-public-method" revision 2
.description "Document each public Python method with a docstring describing its behavior, arguments and return value."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff D102 (pydocstyle): a public method of a public class with no docstring. Dunder methods are D105 and
// `__init__` is D107, except `__new__` and `__call__`, which are D102. Not checked: `@overload` and
// `@override` methods, `@x.setter`/`@x.deleter` (private), defs decorated with a `pydocstyle.ignore-decorators`
// entry, and `.pyi` stubs.
//   class C:
//       """Doc."""
//       def run(self): pass    ← D102 at `run`
//       def __call__(self): …  ← D102
#include "python/docstrings.rr"

.violation D102(at: node, x: symbol) code "D102"
    "Add a docstring as the first statement of method `{x}` describing what it does, its arguments and return value; if it overrides a documented base method, decorate it with `@override` instead."
    suppress ruff "D102"
D102(nm, x) :- doc_missing(_, "method", nm, x), (!dunder(x) ; x = "__new__" ; x = "__call__").